<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Taraba State</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Taraba State is a state in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>, created in 1991 from part of Gongola State, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jalingo">Jalingo</a>. Named after the Taraba River, it lies along the Benue and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cameroon">Cameroon</a> border and includes the Mambilla Plateau. It is home to the Jukun kingdom of Wukari and the Muri <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a>, among many other peoples.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/taraba-state.jpg" alt="Taraba State" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dotun55 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chappal_Wadi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
